  ],
  "comments": [
    {
      "paragraph_index": 2,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 3,
      "comment": "Dissolve ingredients except yeast extract, vitamins and sulfide. Adjust pH to 4.5 with H2SO4 and sparge medium with 100% CO2 gas for 30 - 45 min to make it anoxic. Dispense medium under same gas atmosphere into anoxic Hungate-type tubes or serum vials and autoclave. Add yeast extract, vitamins (sterilized by filtration) and sulfide from sterile anoxic stock solutions prepared under 100% N2 gas. The sulfide stock solution (3% w/v) should be neutralized before use (see medium 28). The pH of the complete medium should be at 4.5."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 4,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 7,
      "comment": "First dissolve FeCl2 in the HCl, then dilute in water, add and dissolve the other salts. Finally make up to 1000.00 ml."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 8,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 10,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 12,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 13,
      "comment": "The sulfide solution is prepared in a 250 ml screw-capped bottle with a butyl rubber septum and a magnetic stirrer. The solution is bubbled with nitrogen gas, closed and autoclaved for 15 min. at 121°C. After cooling to room temperature the pH is adjusted to about 7.0 by adding of sterile 2 M H2SO4 drop-wise with a syringe without opening the bottle."
    }
  ]
}